comments.body:
@jamorham
While we're on the subject, I'm finding throughout my testing, Nov. 2 nightly is the most accurate especially once calibrated to my freestyle libre meter. Every version I've tried after including Dec. 9 is not as good. The predictions on the latest sit too high for too long and less accurate in terms of calibrations; after multiple calibrations, Dec. 9 nightly deviated almost 20-40 mg/dL higher each time. Nov. 2 nightly after even a week without calibration stays within 5-10 mg/dL to my meter. I feel my blood sugar (highs and lows) more accurately too with it. It also projects changes in glucose fastest/more accurately compared to the recent builds. See my graph - Dec. 9 nightly was off completely 3 times after calibrations. Switched back to Nov. 2 on last calibration where Dec. 9 version said I was around 282, but meter read 214 (I took Humalog correction so I know it was dropping as intended) and it's been consistent and correct ever since from 6pm onward. 

